   "title": "Two Lights in the Dark",
   "mood": "curious",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "text": "Nevada is bigger than Great Britain. About three million people live in it. And almost nine out of ten of them live in just two places: Las Vegas in the far south, and Reno up against the mountains in the west. Everything in between, hundreds of miles of it, is almost empty. At night, from orbit, you can see it. Two lights, and darkness.",
