    {
     "text": "It is not that nobody ever tried. A lake nearly as big as Lake Erie once filled the northwest of this state, and it vanished. Towns of thousands rose on silver and gold, and blew away within a few years. And today the federal government owns about four fifths of the land, including a stretch of desert it used to set off nuclear bombs. So why does almost nobody live in most of Nevada? There are five reasons. The first one is a wall.",
