    {
     "text": "This is called a rain shadow, and Nevada lives in it. The government's climate scientists put it bluntly: Nevada is the nation's driest state. Across the whole state, the average is about ten inches of rain and snow a year. In the southern lowlands it is closer to four. Up on the high peaks of the Sierra it is more than fifty. Same air, a few dozen miles apart.",
