  {
   "title": "The Water Goes Nowhere",
   "mood": "curious",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "text": "Reason two. What little water there is goes nowhere. Almost all of Nevada lies inside the Great Basin, the largest region in North America where rivers never reach the sea. Rain that falls here stays here. It runs downhill into a valley and stops, and the sun takes it back. Look at the Humboldt River. It rises in the mountains of northeast Nevada and crosses almost the whole state, about three hundred miles. And then it simply ends, in a dry flat called the Humboldt Sink.",
